# Shatter — The gravity well

This file defines the pull the star exerts: the law, the bodies it acts on, and
the bodies it never touches. The star's position and its core are in
`specs/field.md`, and the tick the pull is applied in is in `specs/simulation.md`.

## The law

Every tick, each pulled body gains an acceleration toward the star's centre:

```
d     = the distance from the body's centre to (STAR_X, STAR_Y)
dEff  = max(d, SOFTEN)
aMag  = MU / (dEff * dEff)
a     = aMag, directed along the unit vector from the body to the star's centre
```

`MU` is `4 500 000` and `SOFTEN`, the softening radius, is `90`. Inside `SOFTEN`
the magnitude is capped at `MU / (SOFTEN * SOFTEN)`, so a body approaching the
core is pulled no harder than a body at `d = 90`.

| Distance | Acceleration |
| --- | --- |
| `d = 200` | `112.5` |
| `d = 150` | `200` |
| `d = 120` | `312.5` |
| `d <= 90` | `555.6` (the cap) |

The pull uses the body's direct vector to `(STAR_X, STAR_Y)`, not a wrapped one,
so a body near a corner is pulled by its full distance across the field rather
than by the distance to a wrapped image of the star.

## Which bodies are pulled

| Body | Pulled |
| --- | --- |
| A bullet the ship fired | Yes |
| A saucer bullet | Yes |
| A rock, of any size | Yes |
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
| The ship | No |
| The saucer | No |
| A torpedo | No |
{{else}}
| The ship | No |
| The saucer | No |
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
The ship, the saucer, and the torpedo are powered craft with their own drive. The
well never adds anything to their velocity, whatever their distance from the star,
so each holds exactly the course it is steering.
{{else}}
The ship and the saucer are powered craft with their own drive. The well never
adds anything to their velocity, whatever their distance from the star, so each
holds exactly the course it is steering.
{{/if}}
